- gen0 keeps structs inline with value semantics; ngen modeled them as heap
  objects, so `p2 = p1; p2.a = 100` mutated the shared object. GenCloneIfStruct
  now clones struct-typed values (alloc + memcpy of descriptor word and fields)
  at every storage boundary: var-decl initialization, plain assignment, argument
  passing (fixed, default-filled, variadic tail and bundle passthrough), return
  statements, and List.Add elements. Register order bug in the first draft (the
  size load clobbered x0 before the source push) caught by lldb memmove fault.
