2026-09-14 04:10 slice 37: List operation family, element member access, const
- List<T> gains RemoveAt/Insert/Reverse/IndexOf/AddRange/ToArray as runtime
  helpers over the inline-sequence layout (count/cap/data of 8-byte slots):
  insert shifts with memmove and grows by doubling; addrange grows once and
  self-appends safely; toarray produces a gen0-layout array; indexof compares
  strings by strcmp and everything else field-wise/pointer.
- IndexOf/Contains now share one inline find loop (GenListFind) with
  per-element-kind equality: strcmp for strings, the element's declared
  op_eq when present, field-wise compare for plain structs, register compare
  for primitives.
- struct elements of List/array resolve their members (ElemTyOf no longer
  excludes structs) -- element reads yield the object pointer, writes store
  through it; values clone at storage boundaries since slice 36.
- `const` locals parse (the keyword token is dropped at statement level,
  the ordinary variable path handles the initializer); `const` fields imply
  static (C# semantics).
- encoding lessons baked into the runtime helpers: AAPCS64 variadic values
  travel on the stack; negative-offset loads must use LDUR (LdrU is the
  unsigned form); SUBS/ADD shifted-register words are computed in Zan
  expressions, not hand-packed hex; callee-saved registers must be saved.
- verification: 9 targeted tests vs gen0 all PASS; kernels 27/27; EH green.
